Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Iron Rails Cough Salt
- Story & Context: When the final Svalbard supply locomotive broke its axle on the coastal cliff-track during the first blizzard of October, engineer Magnus abandoned his cargo to drag a single crate of synthesizer oscillator chips through two miles of drifting snow into the Cape Thordsen lamp-room. As the station's kerosene heater sputtered its oily, sickening soot across the linoleum, K-Roc patched the chips into a thawed LinnDrum while MC Beacon-Black tested the shortwave mic with a furious, rhythmic chant directed at the stranded sailors offshore. The resulting broadcast captured the squeal of the derailed freight cars grinding against frozen salt spray, immortalized in the opening hook: "The locomotive snapped, the iron spine went cold, now grab the open wire for the story being told."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Album cover art featuring an abandoned black steam locomotive half-submerged in Arctic coastal sea ice, iron tracks twisting into frothing dark water beneath an ominous sky, textured film grain, muted charcoal and rust tones.

Track 2: Stationmaster Einar’s Pocketwatch
- Story & Context: Sitting in the drafty telegraph shanty at the terminus of the polar rail spur, Stationmaster Einar confessed into the open beacon-microphone that he had deliberately stamped the final departure manifest with a false time just to strand himself with the broadcast crew for the winter. The only rhythmic backing was the erratic mechanical tick of his brass pocketwatch amplified through a ceramic contact mic, suddenly detonated by a massive, gothic Moog bass pulse that shook loose flakes of dried whitewash from the ceiling beams. With the smell of stale coffee and whale tallow heavy in the frozen air, he traded the ticking pocketwatch for the microphone to utter his solitary hook: "I stamped the ledger crooked so the last train couldn't blow, now I rhyme until the thaw breaks through the undertow."
