Track 3: Where Does the Night-Express Terminate?
- Story & Context: Long after the winter ended and search crews finally unlocked the frozen iron hatch of the Cape Thordsen beacon, they found the broadcast room entirely empty except for an endless magnetic tape loop playing over an Oberheim DMX kick drum that was still thumping through the dead transmitter. Legend among maritime radio operators says the trio climbed aboard a spectral phantom coal train that ran straight off the cliff-edge into the Barents Sea, leaving only their voices encoded into the navigational beacon's frequency. Dockworkers at the mainland depot swear that whenever the northern lights ignite the sky, shortwave radio receivers pick up a faint, bouncing rhyme echoing over a church organ: "Where does the night-express terminate its run, when the tracks become the water and we never see the sun?"
